{#
  An embedded archive.org player, as written in wiki page bodies.

  Attributes are rendered with Jinja's `xmlattr` rather than joined by hand.
  The Templetor version built them as `' '.join('%s="%s"' % (k, v))` and spliced
  the result in unescaped, so a value containing a double quote closed the
  attribute and anything after it became real markup -- an `onload=` handler,
  for one. `xmlattr` escapes each value and, since Jinja 3.1.5, rejects keys
  containing whitespace, `/`, `>` or `=`.

  The allowlist is unchanged on purpose, https:// included: it is the behaviour
  this port is required to preserve, not fix. See the scope note on #14387.
#}
{% macro iframe(url, attrs={}) %}
    {% if url.startswith("http://www.archive.org/") or url.startswith("http://archive.org/") or url.startswith("//archive.org/") %}
        <iframe src="{{ url }}"{{ attrs | xmlattr }}></iframe>
    {% endif %}
{% endmacro %}
{#- Rendering this file directly (from the Templetor wrapper) draws the iframe.
    Guarded so that importing the macro does not render the body, which would
    raise on the undefined `url` under StrictUndefined. -#}
{%- if url is defined %}
    {{ iframe(url, attrs | default({})) }}
{%- endif %}
